1. Non-Negotiable Engineering Rules
1.1 Platform & Architecture
Native Windows 11 desktop application using PySide6 only (no HTML, WebView, FastAPI, Flask, Electron, or browser UI).
Strict Core/UI separation: core, intelligence, conversations, memory, agents, voice, vision, tools, security, and database must never import PySide6.
UI communicates with Core exclusively through defined controllers, services, and typed EventBus events.
Preserve existing working modules; inspect before editing; no unnecessary rewrites.
1.2 Privacy & Cloud Restrictions
Local-first by default: Ollama is the primary local provider; Groq is an explicitly consented cloud fallback.
Groq receives ONLY: JARVIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT + the current user message (2 messages). No conversation history, memories, RAG chunks, tool outputs, biometrics, or hidden context.
SHA-256 fingerprint-bound, per-request consent: bound to exact provider, model, and canonical payload; verified immediately before dispatch; expires and never carries over across retries.
1.3 Security
Fail-closed architecture; default-deny for dangerous capabilities; explicit approval before consequential actions.
Pre-execution permission checks + CommandAllowlist.
Append-only audit_log with database-level UPDATE/DELETE protection.
Windows DPAPI for secrets and biometric embeddings (no plaintext secrets in config, logs, DB, or diagnostic exports).
1.4 Implementation Discipline
One stage at a time; never advance until the current stage passes its verification gate.
Never weaken security/privacy contracts or test assertions.
Never modify the jarvis development database during testing; use isolated jarvis_test only.
